- Create an advertisement.
- Upload an advertisement image.
- Preview the advertisement.
- Edit advertisement content.
- Replace the image.
- Set advertisement title.
- Set optional description.
- Configure a destination URL.
- Enable or disable the advertisement.
- Set display position.
- Configure publication dates, if supported.
- Configure display frequency.
- Set an appropriate display priority.
- Delete advertisements.
- Preview the advertisement as a visitor would see it.

Use the actual project architecture and business requirements.

## 7.2 Public Advertisement Display

When an eligible visitor enters the website, the configured advertisement should appear according to its display rules.

Support an appropriate display format, such as:

- Modal advertisement
- Popup advertisement
- Promotional overlay

Choose the format based on the existing website design and avoid damaging the user experience.

## 7.3 Close Button

Every dismissible advertisement must have a clearly visible Close Button.

When a visitor clicks Close:

- The advertisement must disappear immediately.
- The underlying website must remain usable.
- The visitor must not be redirected unexpectedly.
- The advertisement must not immediately reopen because of a component re-render.

Implement appropriate dismissal behavior.

Consider using session-based dismissal or a configurable frequency policy.

Do not create an infinite advertisement popup loop.

## 7.4 Advertisement Display Rules

Implement appropriate display controls.

For example:

- Only active advertisements can appear.
- Future advertisements must not appear early.
- Expired advertisements must not appear.
- Display priorities must be respected.
- The same advertisement must not repeatedly interrupt the visitor.
- Mobile and desktop layouts must be appropriate.
- Closing an advertisement must work on both desktop and mobile.

If multiple advertisements are eligible, use a deterministic selection or priority system.

Avoid showing multiple intrusive popups simultaneously.

## 7.5 Advertisement Destination

If an advertisement has a destination URL:

- Validate it appropriately.
- Use safe link handling.
- Prevent unsafe URL schemes.
- Open external destinations safely when appropriate.

## 7.6 Advertisement Analytics

Where appropriate, track:

- Impressions
- Clicks
- Dismissals

Store analytics through the backend.

Do not count a single impression multiple times because of component re-renders.

Do not trust arbitrary client-provided analytics values without validation and abuse protection.

Do not fabricate impression or click statistics.

